<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<document>
<header>
  <title>Preview Help</title>
</header>

<chapter id="pictures" name="Looking at pictures" keywords="image photo zoom rotate slideshow sidebar">
<p>Open a picture from File Viewer, or with <b>File › Open</b>. The other
pictures in its folder are listed down the sidebar: click one, or press
<kbd>↑</kbd> and <kbd>↓</kbd>, to go through them. Type in the search
field to list only those whose names match.</p>

<aside>
  <h2>From the keyboard</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><td><kbd>⌘+</kbd> <kbd>⌘-</kbd></td><td>Zoom in, zoom out</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>⌘0</kbd></td><td>Fit the window</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>⌘1</kbd></td><td>Actual size</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>⌘L</kbd> <kbd>⌘R</kbd></td><td>Rotate left, right</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>⌘I</kbd></td><td>Info</td></tr>
  </table>
</aside>

<p><b>Rotate</b> turns the picture a quarter. Preview saves it turned
with <kbd>⌘S</kbd>, or asks when you close it or go to another picture.</p>

<p><b>Info</b> shows the picture's size, format and colour, and, for a
photo, when and with what camera it was taken.</p>

<p>The <b>slideshow</b> shows the folder's pictures full screen, one every
few seconds. <kbd>←</kbd> and <kbd>→</kbd> go back and on,
<kbd>Space</kbd> pauses, <kbd>Esc</kbd> ends it.</p>
</chapter>

<chapter id="pdf" name="Reading a PDF" keywords="pdf search find copy text select pages">
<p>A PDF's pages are listed down the sidebar; click one to go to it.
Pages stay sharp at any zoom.</p>

<p>To <b>search</b>, type in the search field. Every match is marked on the
pages, and the status bar says how many there are. The arrows beside the
field, or <kbd>⌘G</kbd> and <kbd>⇧⌘G</kbd>, go from one to the next.</p>

<p>To <b>copy text</b>, drag across it, then press <kbd>⌘C</kbd>, or click
it with the right button and choose <b>Copy</b>. <b>Search for</b> in the
same menu looks for what you selected.</p>
</chapter>

<chapter id="export" name="Saving a copy" keywords="export save png jpeg tiff pdf size">
<p><b>File › Export</b> saves a copy as PNG, JPEG, TIFF or PDF, full size
or half size. For JPEG, the <b>Quality</b> slider trades size for detail.
The size the copy will be is shown before you save it.</p>

<p>For a PDF, PNG, JPEG and TIFF save the page you are looking at as a
picture; PDF saves the whole document.</p>
</chapter>
</document>
